Finding: federated SAML SSO for a gallery app (Salesforce) configures and saves cleanly on
Entra ID Free, with a real auto-generated signing certificate and a live servicePrincipal object
reflecting preferredSingleSignOnMode: "saml". No license refusal encountered at any point in this
flow — contrary to CURRICULUM.md's Recalled assumption that "SAML SSO for non-gallery apps"
requires P1 (that assumption was specifically about non-gallery apps, and is not contradicted by
this result, but the broader intuition that SAML SSO generally needs a premium tier is). This
matches Microsoft's documented Free-tier allowance of federated SSO for a limited number of
gallery apps, now demonstrated directly rather than read off a comparison table.
